From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the desk's windows turn inside the shell's wipe

A theme change now turns the chrome first and the windows once every
shell has captured the frame its wipe starts from, so the wipe passes
across windows turning inside it. DomicileHost says so with a second
event, `windowstheme`, carrying the same DomicileThemeEvent as `theme`.

One name in Chromium's event registry is all it needs here; the member,
the mojom and the dispatch are the fork's own files.
---
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/event_type_names.json5 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/event_type_names.json5 b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/event_type_names.json5
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/event_type_names.json5
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/event_type_names.json5
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
     "battery",
     "clipboard",
     "theme",
+    "windowstheme",
     "filepreview",
     "focuschanged",
     "focusrequested",
